  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Reuses a sealed conditional class/unit terminal for the existing unconditional Minkowski suffix. Mutable unit, torsion, regulator, and saturation wrappers are reconstructed from private hash-bound authority; a reserve/commit/release lease prevents reentrancy and supports retry after suffix failure. Resource/controller requests including max_checkpoint_bytes bypass reuse. The unsafe second public IdealClassGroup field cache from the source commit is removed.",
    "risks": [
      "The live terminal receipt is in-process authority only; detached checkpoints continue through full canonical decoding and verification.",
      "The C4 quintic unconditional suffix remains mathematically expensive (about 27 seconds measured here), although its conditional snapshot overhead is only about 1.4 percent."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Design any future O(1) public IdealClassGroup projection cache as a context-owned immutable-core feature rather than a second unauthenticated field cache.",
